{"id":"n5-127","title":"ほとんど〜","romaji":"hotondo〜","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Used to express 'almost', 'nearly', or 'most'.","longExplanation":"The ほとんど〜 grammar point is used to express that something is 'almost', 'nearly', or 'most'. It can appear in both negative contexts (hardly/barely) or positive contexts (almost all). It is typically followed by a verb or used with a noun to describe the quantity or extent of something.","formation":"ほとんど + Verb / ほとんど + Noun","examples":[{"jp":"彼女はほとんど英語を話せません。","romaji":"Kanojo wa hotondo eigo o hanasemasen.","en":"She can hardly speak English.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ほとんど","vocabId":"1522050","reading":"ほとんど"},{"surface":"英語","vocabId":"1174420","reading":"えいご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話せません","vocabId":"1562360","reading":"はなせません","baseForm":"話せる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2]},{"jp":"ほとんどの人がパーティーに出席しました。","romaji":"Hotondo no hito ga paatii ni shusseki shimashita.","en":"Most people attended the party.","words":[{"surface":"ほとんどの人","vocabId":"1011670","reading":"ほとんどのひと"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"パーティー","vocabId":null},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"出席","vocabId":"1339460","reading":"しゅっせき"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"私たちはほとんど勉強しないでテストに合格しました。","romaji":"Watashitachi wa hotondo benkyou shinaide tesuto ni goukaku shimashita.","en":"We passed the test with hardly any studying.","words":[{"surface":"私たち","vocabId":"1311300","reading":"わたしたち"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ほとんど","vocabId":"1522050","reading":"ほとんど"},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface